==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|upheven|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|uphebban|ūphebban|lang=ang}}, {{term|upahebban|ūpāhebban|to lift up, raise up, exalt, rise in the air, fly|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{prefix|up|heave|lang=-}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|opheffen||to lift, raise|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|aufheben||to lift, raise, cancel, repeal|lang=de}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|upheaves|upheaving|upheaved}} (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')

# {{transitive}} To [[heave]] or [[lift]] up; [[raise]] up or [[aloft]].
# {{transitive}} To [[lift]] or [[thrust]] something [[upward]] [[forcefully]], or be similarly lifted or thrust upward.
# {{intransitive}} To be lifted up; [[rise]].

